note The .codemap-cache file: every indexed file's symbols, calls, targets, references, imports and highlight spans, keyed by the file's text hash. Derived from the backends and never committed. It exists so a launch does not wait on a server or a parse; anything it cannot answer is re-derived. It is the io-cache crate: CacheStore is its surface, wire.rs mirrors the bytes (the Cached* structs, Reader, Writer) and convert.rs maps them to and from the domain's SourceFile, so the index model changes without changing the format.

